	"review-publish": $("Review / Publish", "Prepare the owned final Draft and staged effects for review or automatic application after Send.", "Connect the final owned Draft in Response, either in Main or inside a static subgraph.", "Inspect the reply and proposed effects in Preview, then Apply reviewed candidate to accept the root result or reject it. Manual review is the default.", "In Details, enable Automatically apply revised reply to add and select a revised reply swipe after a successful Send, preserving the original and accepting its connected story changes.", "Enable Automatically accept story changes to save connected staged effects when the final reply is unchanged, using the existing native swipe. This separate opt-in runs only after a successful Send; previews, cancellation, stale sources and ambiguous reviews cannot save automatically."),
	format: $("Format", "Validate and serialize explicit records as JSON, JSON Lines, CSV, text, or Markdown.", "Choose Records or raw JSON Text input and connect the matching value.", "Choose serialization, field mapping, and any schema or CSV columns.", "Inspect Records, Text, and the report before connecting a file mutation."),
	"read-file": $("Read File", "Reuse saved data or initialize a managed story document, returning its text, parsed value, document wrapper, and live write reference.", "When no file is set, Generate from story uses one bounded request with this node’s model, current conversation and character. Existing files and saved chat data are reused first.", "Choose Valid starting template to use schema-valid initial state without a request, or Require a file to choose an authorized source. Initialization instructions and completion limit are in File. Initialized contents save only when you accept the reviewed result.", "Choose a file or Import from device for an independent input copy. A configured source remains authoritative when unavailable. Advanced contains character access and custom locations on the computer running SillyTavern.", "Use Parsed value for structured Data calculations, Document for metadata, Text for transformation, and Reference for an authorized Write to File. Text and Markdown sources skip Parsed value."),
